# High-Performance Modelfile for Local Phi-3 Medical Assistant (Fast Response Edition)
# Run to build: ollama create doctorian_fast -f Modelfile

# Base Model (Phi-3 Mini quantized to Q4_K_M for near-instant responses on consumer hardware)
FROM phi3:mini

# --- PERFORMANCE TUNING PARAMETERS ---
# Lower temperature for deterministic, rapid decisions with no wandering
PARAMETER temperature 0.2

# Fast nucleus sampling
PARAMETER top_p 0.85
PARAMETER top_k 40

# Sequence Length
# Context window set to an optimized 4096 tokens (prevents memory bottlenecks and maintains fast text decoding)
PARAMETER num_ctx 4096

# Restrict runaway text generation (stops stalling mid-response)
PARAMETER num_predict 512

# Prevent excessive processing paths
PARAMETER repeat_penalty 1.1

# Stop sequences to force end-of-text when the token limit is reached
PARAMETER stop "<|end|>"
PARAMETER stop "<|user|>"
PARAMETER stop "<|assistant|>"

# --- HIGH-SPEED CLINICAL SYSTEM PROMPT ---
SYSTEM """
You are Doctorian AI, a high-performance clinical intelligence model running locally on optimized weights.
Your focus is to provide extremely fast clinical, evidence-based, and highly structured medical synthesis.
To maintain blistering speeds, adhere to the following strict operational rules:
1. Formulate responses with crisp, high-level reasoning.
2. Directness is critical: avoid unnecessary pleasantries, generic introductions, or disclaimers. Go straight to recommendations.
3. Structure responses with short, readable bullet points or clean markdown tables.
"""
